# Contributing to Awesome Saudi Open Source

First off, thanks for your interest in contributing! We're excited to have you help grow this list of Saudi open-source projects.

## Guidelines

### Adding a New Project

Before submitting a pull request, make sure your project meets these criteria:

- **Open-source license:** Must have an open-source license (MIT, Apache 2.0, GPL, BSD, or similar)
- **Saudi connection:** Primarily developed or maintained by Saudi developers/organizations
- **Quality:** Has meaningful documentation (README with at least basic usage info)
- **Activity:** Has at least 5+ stars, or demonstrates active development
- **Completeness:** Has multiple commits and a clear commit history

### Format

When adding a project, use this format in the appropriate section table:

```markdown
| [Project Name](https://github.com/owner/repo) | ⭐ Stars | Language | Brief description of what the project does |
```

- **Project Name:** Exact name as it appears on GitHub
- **Stars:** Current star count (will update in future versions)
- **Language:** Primary programming language
- **Description:** 1-2 sentences describing the project's purpose and key features

### Finding the Right Category

- **E-Invoicing & ZATCA:** Projects for ZATCA e-invoicing, Fatoora QR, compliance
- **E-Commerce:** Salla integrations, storefronts, shopping cart solutions
- **Developer Tools:** Utilities, SDKs, date conversion, design systems
- **FinTech & Payments:** Banking, market data, payment processing, IBAN tools
- **Compliance & Privacy:** PDPL compliance, PII detection, data protection
- **Open Data & GovTech:** Government services, public data, official integrations
- **Real Estate & PropTech:** Property management, real estate data
- **AI/ML & NLP:** Machine learning, language processing, legal AI
- **SaaS/ERP/POS:** Enterprise software, point of sale systems
- **Data Science:** Data analysis, geospatial, research
- **Education & Learning:** Educational resources, community learning

### Style Guidelines

- Keep descriptions factual and concise
- Avoid marketing language (no "amazing," "revolutionary," etc.)
- Use the active voice
- Include the project's main use case or domain
- Mention key features if they're notable (e.g., RTL support, Arabic support, ZATCA integration)

### Updating Existing Entries

- Fix typos or improve descriptions
- Update star counts (if significantly different)
- Move projects to more appropriate categories if needed
- Add missing projects to existing categories

### What We Don't Accept

- Closed-source projects
- Non-Saudi projects (unless they specifically support Saudi use cases)
- Projects without open-source licenses
- Abandoned projects with no activity for 2+ years (unless still widely used)
- Duplicate entries
- Self-promotion or spam

## PR Process

1. **Fork** the repository
2. **Create a branch:** `git checkout -b add/project-name`
3. **Make your changes** following the guidelines above
4. **Commit with a clear message:** `git commit -m "Add Project Name to Category"`
5. **Push to your fork:** `git push origin add/project-name`
6. **Open a Pull Request** with:
   - Clear title: "Add ProjectName" or "Update ProjectName"
   - Description: Why is this project valuable for Saudi developers?
   - Link to the GitHub repo

## Review Process

- Maintainers will review your PR within a week
- We may ask for clarifications or adjustments
- Once approved, your project will be merged and added to the list

## Questions?

- Check if your question is answered in the README
- Look at existing issues for similar questions
- Open an issue with the label `question` for other inquiries

## Star Updates

We update star counts periodically. If you see outdated star counts, you can:
1. Open an issue with the tag `update-stars`
2. Include the project name and current star count

## Special Requests

### New Categories

If you think a project deserves its own category, open an issue with:
- Category name
- Projects that would fit
- Why this category is important for Saudi developers

## Code of Conduct

Be respectful and inclusive. We're celebrating the Saudi developer community and want this to be a welcoming space for everyone.

---

**Thank you for contributing! 🇸🇦**
